; =============================================================================
; PANEL MEMORY - FACTORY BANK NAMES + 80 FACTORY PRESET RECORDS
; =============================================================================
; ROM range 0x99EC00-0x9ABF3F.  Factory contents of the PANEL MEMORY feature
; (one-touch panel registrations; Matsushita debug names in the maincpu use
; the "Pmem" prefix, e.g. PmemOutLGridCheck): 10 themed banks of 8 presets,
; selected with the 8 PANEL MEMORY buttons.
;
; LAYOUT:
;   0x99EC00  PanelMemory_BankNames   10 x 16-char space-padded bank names
;   0x99ECA0  PanelMemory_Preset_00   80 x 674-byte preset records
;             ..PanelMemory_Preset_79   (record i = bank i/8, button i%8+1)
;
; CONSUMERS (v10 maincpu; same code in v7/v9 at shifted addresses -- these
; routines still carry placeholder names, rename when that region of the
; program ROM is converted):
;   LABEL_FC81EF  init-all: MEM_COPY(0x1ED350, 0xEDBA1C, 16) [spare name
;                 slot, "HK " signature], MEM_COPY(0x1ED360, 0x99EC00, 160)
;                 [the 10 bank names], then calls LABEL_FC7DD8 for i=0..79
;   LABEL_FC7E82  copy bank name i (i<10) to RAM 0x1ED360+16*i
;   LABEL_FC7DD8  build the 960-byte RAM record at 0x1ED400+960*i:
;                   memcpy(ram+0x000, rom_rec+0x00, 0x7c)   name + parts 0-3
;                   memcpy(ram+0x07c, 0xEDB478,     0x11e)  parts 4-14 come
;                     from a fixed default block in the program ROM (the ROM
;                     record does not store them)
;                   memcpy(ram+0x19a, rom_rec+0x7c, 0x226)  parts 15-25 +
;                     global chunks
;
; RECORD FORMAT - a stream of (tag, length, payload[length]) chunks; a 0xff
; tag byte terminates the stream and one more 0xff byte pads the record to
; 674 bytes.  Emitted below as one line per chunk: tag in hex, length in
; decimal, payload in hex.  All 80 records carry the same 34-chunk sequence:
;   0x78/18       16-char preset name + 2 spare bytes (always 0x00 0x00)
;   0x00-0x03/24  sound-part parameter blocks (the four realtime parts);
;                 the RAM image continues with parts 0x04-0x0e from the
;                 program-ROM default block, so tags 0x00-0x19 form one
;                 26-part space
;   0x0f-0x16,0x19/24  nine more part blocks (accompaniment/rhythm side)
;   0x43/4 0x44-0x46/10 0x47/8 0x48/10   parameter groups (undecoded)
;   0x90/6 0x60/4                        parameter groups (undecoded)
;   0x61,0x63-0x66/24                    part-block-sized groups (undecoded)
;   0x68/10 0x70/8 0x72/14 0x92/14 0x71/2 0x99/30 0x80/14  (undecoded)
;
; PART-BLOCK FIELD OBSERVATIONS (24-byte payload, from cross-record diffs):
;   +0/+1  sound selection (program number + bank/group byte)
;   +3     volume-like level 0x3c-0x7f
;   +8/+9  0x40-centred pair (pan-like)
;   +13    part/routing byte, constant per part across all 80 records:
;          equals the part number for parts 0x00-0x03 and 0x0f, and is
;          0xc0|n for parts 0x10-0x16 (0x19 is 0xcf except in preset 15)
; =============================================================================

